                  <p class="text-sm text-steel-600">Village cooperative / small workshop → <b>HN325</b> (best seller, hot press mainstay for peanut, cold press also possible, entry recommended). <br>Mid-size oil mill / toll processor → <b>HN355 / HN400</b>.<br>Large factory / bulk exporter → <b>HN426 / HN480 / HN500</b>.<br><span class="text-xs text-steel-500">For small-scale trial HN300 is possible but has limited daily volume, not our main recommendation.</span></p>
                </div>
                <div class="pl-5 ml-3 border-l-[3px] border-blue-400 py-4 relative"><span class="absolute -left-[10px] top-5 w-[15px] h-[15px] rounded-full bg-steel-900 border-[3px] border-white box-content"></span>
                  <h5 class="font-bold text-steel-800 mb-1">Step 2: What seed do you press? (Hardness → tonnage)</h5>
                  <p class="text-sm text-steel-600">Soft–medium: peanut, rapeseed, soybean, sunflower, castor, flax → 300–400 real tons sufficient (HN325/355/400).<br>Sesame specialist → HN325/355 Sesame (300 mm small barrel).<br>Medium-hard: tea seed, walnut, flaxseed, almond → 400–500 real tons (HN400/426).<br>Super-hard: copra, hemp seed, pine nut → 500–630 real tons (HN480/500) + consider 300 mm small barrel.<br>Special feeds: fresh coconut meat → 300 Type Coconut; oil sludge / spent bleaching earth / fruit & veg dehydration → HN325LB.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="pl-5 ml-3 border-l-[3px] border-blue-400 py-4 relative"><span class="absolute -left-[10px] top-5 w-[15px] h-[15px] rounded-full bg-steel-900 border-[3px] border-white box-content"></span>
                  <h5 class="font-bold text-steel-800 mb-1">Step 3: How many kg per day? (→ single vs double barrel)</h5>
                  <p class="text-sm text-steel-600">Tens of kg / day trial → standard single-barrel 390 mm is sufficient.<br>Hundreds of kg / day → consider <b>double-barrel</b> option (still choose base model by seed type; only add double-barrel configuration).<br>1+ tons / day → definitely <b>double-barrel</b> (available for any model) or multiple machines in parallel. Note: daily volume does not decide which base model to pick.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="pl-5 ml-3 border-l-[3px] border-blue-400 py-4 relative"><span class="absolute -left-[10px] top-5 w-[15px] h-[15px] rounded-full bg-steel-900 border-[3px] border-white box-content"></span>
                  <h5 class="font-bold text-steel-800 mb-1">Step 4: Budget and space</h5>
                  <p class="text-sm text-steel-600">Tight budget / small space → start with HN325, add more machines later.<br>Comfortable budget / hardened floor available → jump straight to HN480/500 double-barrel.<br>Note: HN480/500 weigh 3+ tons — confirm door width, crane access, floor load-bearing.</p>
                </div>
